dia.org/wiki/J%C3%A4mtland","c":3},{"y":1217,"t":"capital_move","x":"1217: Bergen is the capital again, as the civil wars end.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Norway_(872–1397)","c":3},{"y":1261,"t":"gain","x":"1261: the Norse settlements in Greenland subordinate themselves to the Norwegian crown.","cp":"norse-greenland","cpn":"Norse Greenland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norse_Greenland","c":3},{"y":1263,"t":"contest_start","x":"1263: Norway and Scotland fight at Largs over the Hebrides and Mann.","cp":"kingdom-of-alba","cpn":"Kingdom of Alba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Perth","c":2},{"y":1264,"t":"gain","x":"1264: Iceland swears to the King of Norway.","cp":"icelandic-commonwealth","cpn":"Icelandic Commonwealth","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelandic_Commonwealth","c":3},{"y":1266,"t":"contest_end","x":"1266: the Treaty of Perth ends the dispute over the isles.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-alba","cpn":"Kingdom of Alba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Perth","c":3},{"y":1266,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1266: the Hebrides and the Isle of Man pass to Scotland.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-the-isles","cpn":"Kingdom of the Isles","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Perth","c":3},{"y":1306,"t":"gain","x":"1306: Norway builds Vardøhus in the far east of Finnmark.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Norway_(872–1397)","c":2},{"y":1314,"t":"capital_move","x":"1314: the capital moves to Oslo.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Norway_(872–1397)","c":3},{"y":1319,"t":"rename","x":"1319: the Fairhair line ends and Magnus Eriksson, king of Sweden, is acknowledged king of Norway.","m":8,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnus_IV_of_Sweden","c":3},{"y":1343,"t":"rename","x":"1343: Haakon VI is made king of Norway.","m":8,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnus_IV_of_Sweden","c":3},{"y":1380,"t":"rename","x":"1380: Olaf IV inherits Norway on top of Denmark.","m":9,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalmar_Union","c":3},{"y":1387,"t":"rename","x":"1387: Margaret becomes regent of Norway and Denmark.","m":8,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalmar_Union","c":3},{"y":1389,"t":"rename","x":"1389: Eric of Pomerania is proclaimed king of Norway.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalmar_Union","c":3},{"y":1397,"t":"dissolve","x":"1397: the Kalmar Union joins Norway, Denmark and Sweden under one crown.","m":6,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalmar_Union","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Battle of Hafrsfjord","from":872,"to":872,"outcome":"Harald Fairhair's victory over Kjotve the Rich and the western kings, traditionally dated 872; the petty kingdoms are united.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harald_Fairhair"},{"name":"Battle of Svolder","from":1000,"to":1000,"outcome":"Olav Tryggvason is killed; 'the Danes recaptured Norway under Sweyn Forkbeard' and the Lade earls rule the west and Trøndelag.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Norway"},{"name":"Battle of Stiklestad","from":1030,"to":1030,"outcome":"Olaf Haraldsson is killed by the locals; Norway is united again under his son Magnus the Good in 1035.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Norway"},{"name":"Magnus III's expedition to the Western Isles","from":1098,"to":1099,"outcome":"The Hebrides and the Isle of Man come under Norway in 1098 ('Edgar of Scotland signed the islands over to Magnus III'); Anglesey, held briefly, reverts to the Welsh in 1099.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Perth"},{"name":"Norwegian civil wars (era)","from":1130,"to":1217,"outcome":"'In 1130, a civil war era broke out over succession to the throne'; the wars 'ended in 1217 with the appointment of Håkon Håkonsson'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Norway"},{"name":"Scottish-Norwegian war over the Hebrides (Battle of Largs)","from":1263,"to":1266,"outcome":"Largs (1263) is inconclusive; Haakon IV dies in Orkney that winter.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Perth"}],"certainty":[{